The implementation of the evaluator will depend upon the @newterm{syntax} of
the expressions to be evaluated being pinned down once, in a parser.  The
parser takes the data the given-code reader produces and maps each datum onto a
typed node: an assignment is no longer a list that happens to begin with the
symbol @code{set!} but a @code{SetE} value whose fields are the variable and
the value expression.  Implementation of expressions will be described in
detail in @ref{4.1.2}.  There are also operations,
described in @ref{4.1.3}, that specify the representation of procedures
and environments.  For example, @code{makeProcedure} constructs compound
procedures, @code{lookup} accesses the values of variables, and
@code{callPrimitive} applies a primitive procedure to a given list
of arguments.

